{# THE CARD EVERY CHART IN THE PRODUCT IS DRAWN IN.

   THE PLATE'S SIBLING: a module states what its series is and this is what
   surrounds it — a title, a fixed box, the caption under it. A chart that
   grew with its data would make one topic's page twice another's, so the
   height is the platform's and a caller may change it only through the same
   custom-property door a plate's height comes through.

   AN EMPTY CHART IS NOT DRAWN. A box with axes and no line in it reads as a
   measurement of nought; here it says, in the house's own words, that
   nobody published a point.

   Rendered by Twig\ChartRuntime, never included by hand — a module writes
   {{ atlas_chart(chart, 'Title') }}. #}
{# THE CONTROLLER IS ON THE PLATE, NOT THE CANVAS. The canvas is UX Chart.js's
   own element and carries its controller; the pre-connect event bubbles to
   this one, which is where a series' category token becomes a colour. #}
<div class="chart-plate" data-controller="{{ controller }}"{% if boxStyle %} style="{{ boxStyle }}"{% endif %}>
    {% if title %}<span class="tab">{{ title }}{% if unit %}<span class="src">&middot; {{ unit }}</span>{% endif %}</span>{% endif %}

    {% if empty %}
        {# NOBODY PUBLISHED A POINT. Not an empty box: a sentence. #}
        <div class="chart-none">
            <b>No figure for this period</b>
            <span>the module that would publish it has nothing to say yet &mdash; which is not a nought</span>
        </div>
    {% else %}
        <div class="chart-box">{{ canvas|raw }}</div>
    {% endif %}

    {# THE CHIP LEGEND: the house pill, one per series, wearing its category
       through the shell's `data-cat` door; a series that still states its
       own swatch hands it to the same `--cat` the door would set; the target
       is the idle pill, because a dashed grey line is not a category. #}
    {% if legend %}
        <div class="chart-legend">
            {%- for row in legend -%}
                {%- if row.cat is not null -%}
                    <span class="chip" data-cat="{{ row.cat }}">{{ row.label }}</span>
                {%- elseif row.swatch is not null -%}
                    <span class="chip" style="--cat:{{ row.swatch }}">{{ row.label }}</span>
                {%- else -%}
                    <span class="chip idle">{{ row.label }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if caption %}<p class="use">{{ caption }}</p>{% endif %}
</div>
